{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Why do you cry out.</b> Some say that Moses cries out to HaShem, but this is not correct, for He has already spoken to him, 'and I will be honored against Pharaoh' (Exodus 14:4). Rather, 'speak to Moses' is set against all Israel, because the children of Israel cried out to HaShem." "And they journey little by little until they reach the edge of the sea:"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {0 "Resolved פ' ד as a chapter-verse citation, Exodus 14:4, matching the quoted phrase אכבדה בפרעה."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:34:25.239951804Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}